AB  - Lab experiment is increasingly emphasized in science education to enhance students' scientific inquiry capabilities. This study developed a science experiment environment integrating Head-Mounted Display Augmented Reality (HMD AR) with an AI tutor to assist junior high school students in understanding the imaging principles of convex lenses. Preliminary results indicated significant improvements in students' optical conceptual test scores. Additionally, guidance from the AI tutor promoted students' reflective observation during lab experiments. However, students' active interaction with the AI tutor remains limited and requires further enhancement. © 2026 IEEE.
