SP  - 1
EP  - 6
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3772128.3772129
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3772128.3772129
AB  - This paper presents an interactive system designed to facilitate learning of Chaozhou embroidery, a nationally listed intangible cultural heritage representing traditional Chinese craftsmanship. Grounded in constructivist theory, we propose a digital teaching framework emphasizing contextualization, interaction, and hands-on practice. The system collects extensive video documentation of Chaozhou embroidery techniques, trains generative adversarial networks to build an embroidery database, and employs Video Swin Transformer to extract key operations into frame-by-frame tutorials. These animations are projected directly onto fabrics via interactive projection, intuitively guiding users through the distinctive "raised-relief" techniques. By decomposing complex processes into manageable steps with real-time visual feedback, the system significantly enhances beginners' engagement and skill acquisition. This integration of traditional craft with digital innovation opens new avenues for preserving and disseminating Chaozhou culture, promoting sustainable development of this art form.
