AB  - Currently, there is not much research on digital preservation systems that utilize Large Language Models and have strong pertinence and timeliness for Lingnan intangible cultural heritage. This study designed a three-module collaborative digital preservation system for Lingnan intangible cultural heritage based on an adapter-tuned Large Language Model. The system consists of three major modules: data processing and analysis, display and dissemination, and user interaction. It can process and analyze data of Lingnan intangible cultural heritage, diversely display and disseminate high-quality content, and interact well with users. The content created through this system outperforms traditional cultural heritage promotional materials in multiple engagement metrics, including reading traffic, likes, comments, and shares. © 2025 The Authors.
