AB  - In view of the efficiency bottleneck and lack of artistic expression in children's picture book creation, this study proposes an innovative solution based on improved cyclic generative adversarial network. The traditional design process relies on designers to manually transform photo materials into picture-book style images, facing problems such as long creation cycle, distortion of details and difficulty in compatibility with art specifications. In this paper, we reconstruct the CycleGAN framework by three core techniques: introducing residual dense module into the generator to enhance the ability of extracting detailed features of picture books; using the discriminator of optimized convolution layer to enhance the accuracy of style transfer; innovatively embedding the loss function between color quantity control and CMYK printing specification. The data set verification shows that the improved model is significantly better than the baseline model in PSNR (25.89dB), SSIM (0.93) and other indicators, providing intelligent solutions with artistic expression and production feasibility for creative design.
