AB  - The advancement of Artificial Intelligence (AI) and Augmented Reality (AR) technologies presents new opportunities for immersive architectural visualization, particularly in the context of tropical building design. This study explores the use of generative AI tools to create 3D models of tropical residential architecture from textual prompts, with the goal of integrating these models into mobile WebAR applications. A comparative evaluation was conducted on three generative 3D AI platforms based on visual quality, generation speed, AR format compatibility, and performance in WebAR environments. The research also includes performance benchmarking using frame rate (FPS), polygon count, and file size, supported by AR scene previews. AI generated 3D models produces more than 35,000 polygon count and it runs ranging from 18 to 30 frame per second. This indicates that while all platforms can generate visually compelling models, optimization using another 3D software to reduce polygon count is required to meet mobile AR constraints. The study highlights the most balanced solution and recommends future research in three key areas: technical optimization for mobile WebAR performance, architectural relevance through tropical-specific datasets, and user accessibility via intuitive workflows and tools. © 2025 IEEE.
