AB  - The absence of shared experiences between younger and older individuals widens the generational gap, and often places a strain on familial relationships. This experience aims to bridge the digital divide by inviting all users into an emotionally rich, collaborative design process that combines AI-driven image generation with geo-spatial memory mapping. Through uploading an image, providing prompts to a custom scene generator, and selecting views from Look Around to compare scenes from the past, users may recreate personalized immersive spatial environments, and experience time-enabled geo-spatial navigation paired with soundscapes that reflect the historical and cultural setting of the space. By enabling youth to visually re construct the memories of older adults through collaborative co-creation, this approach integrates storytelling, spatial exploration, and emotional engagement across both local and remote settings, thereby fostering inter-generational connection and understanding.
