TI  - ChartBench: A Comprehensive Evaluation Benchmark for Chart Understanding Capabilities of Vision-Language Models
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings of the 2025 2nd International Conference on Virtual Reality, Image and Signal Processing
SP  - 253
EP  - 257
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3772128.3772169
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3772128.3772169
AB  - Chart understanding poses unique challenges for vision-language models (VLMs), requiring precise numerical information extraction from unlabeled charts through visual spatial reasoning. While current VLMs excel in general visual understanding tasks, they exhibit significant performance degradation in chart understanding, and existing evaluation frameworks lack systematicity and comprehensiveness.To address this, we construct ChartBench, a large-scale benchmark dataset specifically designed for evaluating VLM chart understanding capabilities. ChartBench contains 20 core data distribution patterns with progressive complexity design, from labeled to unlabeled charts, from single-line to complex multi-line and stacked visualizations. Through systematic evaluation of mainstream models including GPT-4o, GLM-4.1V, GPT5-nano, and GPT5, we find that even the most advanced models experience 40-60% drops in numerical extraction accuracy when processing unlabeled complex charts, performing particularly poorly in multi-line and stacked visualization scenarios.Contributions :(i) ChartBench benchmark dataset: Establish the first large-scale evaluation benchmark specifically for chart understanding, covering 20 data distribution patterns and multi-level complexity; (ii) Mainstream model performance insights: Reveal limitations and improvement directions of current state-of-the-art VLMs in chart understanding tasks; (iii) Chart data synthesis framework: Establish comprehensive chart data synthesis techniques, providing reproducible data generation tools for related research.
