AB  - Large Language Models (LLMs) offer significant potential for integration with Virtual Reality (VR), but current AI systems struggle to generate accurate 3D environments and support semantic interaction. We present ChemersiveLLM, a VR-based chemistry learning platform that leverages LLMs for instruction sequencing, natural language grounding, and real-time guidance. Using a semantic action-mapping framework, the system translates AI-generated content into structured lab actions, enabling multimodal interaction, embodied experimentation, and intelligent feedback. Comparative evaluation across textbook, chatbot-based, and VR learning shows that our system improves engagement, comprehension, and satisfaction, underscoring its promise as a next-generation tool for science education. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
