TI  - Computed Tomography Digital Learning In Mixed Reality
PY  - 2025
T2  - 2025 IEEE Gaming, Entertainment, and Media Conference (GEM)
IS  - 2025
SP  - 1
EP  - 4
DO  - 10.1109/GEM66882.2025.11155831
SN  - 2766-6530
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105030924909?origin=resultslist
AB  - This study explores the integration of Serious Games, Mixed Reality, and Large Language Models to enhance learning outcomes in Computed Tomography education. Traditional Computed Tomography training faces challenges such as high equipment costs, limited clinical practice opportunities, and abstract learning content, making it difficult for learners to develop a comprehensive understanding. To achieve these issues, we established a Mixed Reality-based educational system that provides an immersive and interactive learning environment, enabling learners to enhance their understanding through three-dimensional simulated Computed Tomography operations, dynamic image reconstruction, and case-based simulations. The system features component introductions, disassembly animations, and operational process simulations, further enriching the learning experience. Additionally, a Large Language Model-powered question-Answering system is integrated and fine-Tuned using Low-Rank Adaptation, equipping the model with domain-specific Computed Tomography knowledge. This system enables real-Time responses to learner inquiries and enhances engagement through multi-Turn dialogues and personalized learning recommendations. The expected outcomes of this study include improving the learning performance of Computed Tomography theory and operation, enhancing learner motivation and autonomy, and optimizing instructional content through real-Time data tracking and adaptive learning mechanisms. Future research will focus on empirical validation to assess the system's effectiveness in both academic and clinical education settings. Additionally, continuous refinement of the Large Language Model-powered question-Answering system based on user feedback will be conducted to further advance the digitalization and intelligent transformation of Computed Tomography education. © 2025 IEEE.
