AB  - This paper presents a fine-tuned summarization system that applies the React Three Fiber (R3F) method to the text-to-text transfer transformer (T5) model, widely used in the field of text summarization. The goal is to address communication issues by incorporating virtual reality (VR) into a video conferencing platform, which is a collaborative tool that reduces costs and improves efficiency. However, manual summarization is still required because of communication challenges and the lack of a built-in document summarization feature. Therefore, this paper proposes a design and implementation plan for a meeting minute summarization system within the video conferencing platform. The T5 language model was fine-tuned using the proposed technique, and its performance was evaluated using the ROUGE-1, ROUGE-2, and ROUGE-L scores, which measure precision, recall, and F1-score by comparing the overlap between the generated and reference summaries. In future work, we will perform comprehensive statistical analyses using standard significance tests. © This is an Open Access article distributed under the terms of the Creative Commons Attribution Non-Commercial License (http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/3.0/) which permits unrestricted non-commercial use, distribution, and reproduction in any medium, provided the original work is properly cited.
