DO  - 10.1007/978-3-032-05925-3_14
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105021842000?origin=resultslist
AB  - Traditional training methods face challenges such as high costs, operational risks, and limited scalability. Digital twinning enables real-time simulation and optimization, while AI-driven assistants offer personalized instruction. This study explores the development and evaluation of an AI-powered virtual training system, emphasizing its benefits in knowledge acquisition and training performance. It presents the design and implementation of an AI-powered immersive virtual training system to enhance trainee learning in the assembly of machine parts in a virtual environment. The system provides real-time guidance and feedback by integrating Generative AI, Extended Reality (XR), and voice interaction. A virtual assistant, powered by OpenAI’s ChatGPT API, interprets trainee queries and delivers step-by-step instructions. WhisperSpeech-to- Text (STT) and Google Text-to-Speech (TTS) facilitate seamless voice interaction. Built using Unity and tested with an HTC VIVE headset, the system allows trainees to interactively assemble a lathe machine without prior knowledge of its components. The experimental evaluation demonstrated significant improvements in user engagement, task performance, and knowledge retention compared to non-AI-supported training. These findings highlight the potential of AI-integrated digital twins in optimizing industrial training methodologies. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2025.
