TI  - Ecovotive Chimeras
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings - SIGGRAPH Asia 2025 Art Gallery, SA Art Gallery 2025
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3757368.3765558
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105025678142?origin=resultslist
AB  - The project begins with the first ten images retrieved from Google Search of wild animals burned in wildfires across severely affected regions. From these, three chimeras emerge in each of the five continents, from biomes most impacted by fire in North America, South America, Africa, Asia, and Australia, through a process of melting carbonized remains into one another via AI. The algorithmically ranked images—already filtered through machinic logic—are processed through a sequence of generative systems: starting with AI-generated animations created from appropriated photographic material and short text prompts, decomposed into video frames, and then transformed into three-dimensional hybrid forms through AI-based 3D reconstruction. These resulting entities—chimeric, spectral, and ontologically unstable—are materialized via 3D printing in white PLA and accompanied by augmented reality (AR) layers that reveal their internal, data-driven mutations. The bizarre logic of generative AI aesthetics—marked by hallucinated forms, melted boundaries, blurred textures, and indeterminate shapes—becomes a critical dialogue with the visual and biological trauma of wildfire destruction. The dramatic abstraction in generative outputs mirrors the devastation in ecologies like the Amazon biome, Brazil’s wetlands, California, the Republic of Congo, Australia, Mongolia, and beyond. The audience is invited to hold these hybrid beings, feel their fragility, and enter—via AR—a liminal zone where emergence, agency, and entropy converge—an ephemeral retreat of continuous becoming © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
