TI  - Empathy in VR: Immersive Storytelling to Combat Loneliness and Amplify Marginalized Voices
PY  - 2025
T2  - 2025 IEEE International Symposium on Technology and Society (ISTAS)
SP  - 1
EP  - 4
DO  - 10.1109/ISTAS65609.2025.11269640
SN  - 2158-3412
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105030546515?origin=resultslist
AB  - We present Empathy in VR, a conceptual design and prototype that explores how immersive storytelling, generative AI, and virtual reality (VR) can be combined to foster empathy and enhance social connectedness. Developed in collaboration with an artist working closely with marginalized communities, the project enables individuals to co-create personal narratives and AI-generated visual artworks grounded in lived experiences. These multimodal expressions are brought to life in an interactive virtual museum, where visitors engage with the stories through spatialized audio, symbolic artifacts, and immersive 3D environments created using Arrival Space and photogrammetric scanning. Rooted in Human-Computer Interaction (HCI) and affective computing, the system draws on established frameworks of presence, embodiment, and psychological engagement to support both cognitive and affective empathy. The design is guided by principles of emotional resonance, accessibility, and authenticity, with the broader goal of addressing social fragmentation and the loneliness epidemic through immersive, human-centered media. This work contributes to HCI discourse on the ethical and emotional dimensions of emerging technologies. It positions immersive storytelling as a means of inclusive representation and social repair, proposing a vision for AI that prioritizes creative agency, emotional awareness, and shared human understanding. Empathy in VR highlights new directions for designing systems that promote empathy and outlines future plans to incorporate dynamic interactivity and affective feedback to deepen user engagement. ©2025 IEEE.
