EP  - 558
DO  - 10.1007/978-3-031-87704-9_38
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105021004186?origin=resultslist
AB  - The Metaverse is an entirely innovative universe where individuals can explore beyond their limitations, discover their identities and preferences, and form numerous connections similar to our physical world. However, complications arise when experiencing Virtual Reality (VR) within the Metaverse due to the lack of recognition in its digital processes, impacting user well-being. This paper will delve into the evolution of the world inside of communication in the Metaverse, including its origins and the perception of reality in a virtual realm. Moreover, it will discover the advancements in meta-technology and further explain how augmented avatars operate within Virtual Reality through the lens of Ethics and Communication, highlighting issues through real case studies and focusing on data breaches involving AI in Ecuador. To converge these communication challenges involves operating Generative AI processes with Artificial Intelligence-Mediated Communication (AI-MC) as an ethical communication framework for online users. This research aims to cultivate ethical practices and foster effective communication in these ground breaking technological platforms that are set to transform our present and future. © The Author(s), under exclusive license to Springer Nature Switzerland AG 2025.
