AB  - Interactive art appreciation is a method in which multiple participants engage in repeated discussions to interpret artworks. In this approach, a facilitator plays a crucial role by asking questions to the viewers. However, there are currently limited opportunities for facilitator training. To address this, this paper proposes a Mixed Reality (MR) AI system that utilizes MR headsets and a Large Language Model to train facilitators. The system features five virtual viewers, each with distinct personalities and whose facial expressions change through dialogue, allowing users to practice facilitation through interactive dialogue. Contents of what the virtual viewers say are generated by the Large Language Model, GPT-4o. Moreover, in addition to GPT-4o, conversations are conducted using the speech recognition system, Whisper, and the speech synthesis system, Azure Text-To-Speech. © 2025 IEEE.
