AB  - Interior design significantly impacts the aesthetics and functionality of living spaces, yet traditional methods often involve costly consultations, limited visualization options, and complex software. Recent advancements in computer vision techniques for Augmented Reality (AR) and generative models offer transformative potential. This paper introduces Furnit.Ar, a novel mobile application that integrates computer vision algorithms with AR technologies to provide a comprehensive, intuitive, and personalized interior design solution. Furnit.Ar enables users to visualize furniture placement in their physical space using markerless AR with SLAM-based spatial mapping, receive culturally relevant design suggestions based on Vastu Shastra principles via visual-semantic retrieval mechanisms, convert 2D images of real-world objects into usable 3D models through depth estimation and mesh reconstruction, and generate personalized interior design concepts using fine-tuned diffusion models conditioned on scene structure via ControlNet. We detail the system architecture, computer vision methodologies behind each component, dataset construction, and evaluate the performance using Fréchet Inception Distance (FID) metrics, demonstrating a 15.9% improvement over baseline approaches. This work demonstrates the synergistic potential of combining spatial understanding algorithms with generative vision models for creating interactive, visually coherent, and user-centric design tools. © 2025 IEEE.
