AB  - We propose an interactive framework for displaying artificial intelligence (AI) generated 3D meshes in a virtual reality (VR) application that is tailored for clinical rehabilitation in a real-world hospital setting. By streaming multiple state-of-the-art AI models, we parse the verbal instructions of a rehabilitation patient to a personalized 3D mesh for integration into a VR rehabilitation session. Such personalization has the potential to enhance patient engagement via IKEA effect, the psychological phenomenon where individuals show greater engagement and motivation when interacting with content they helped create. The pipeline sequentially converts speech-to-text, text-to-2D image, and image-to-3D mesh, where the VR users can control each step for interactivity and preference. © 2025 IEEE.
