AB  - This study presents a human-AI collaborative workflow to enhance large-scale qualitative thematic analysis. ChatGPT (GPT-4o) supports early coding and theme development, while NotebookLM, using Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG), provides source-grounded validation. Adapting Braun and Clarke's framework with revised phases and role-specific AI tasks, the workflow was tested on 28 interview transcripts from a VR-based National Institutes of Health Stroke Scale (NIHSS) assessment training system. Results from implementation trials and expert feedback indicate improved analytical efficiency, semantic clarity, and interpretive consistency. Rather than replacing human insight, the workflow demonstrates how AI can augment qualitative research by enabling greater scalability, transparency, and contextual alignment in analysis. © 2025 IEEE.
