AB  - Educational systems are in constant transformation, but recent challenges such as the COVID-19 pandemic, the rapid digitization of education, and the emergence of Generative Artificial Intelligence, have placed unprecedented pressure on teaching practices and created an urgent demand for teachers to develop new skills and competences namely to cope with the added stress. Teacher preparation and training must therefore become more effective, better aligned with technological evolution, and supported by innovative didactic approaches. Immersive technologies like Virtual Reality (VR) offer strong potential to enhance cognitive and pedagogical outcomes by increasing both engagement and motivation among trainees. The XRSkills project was designed in response to this need, focusing on soft skills training for teachers and educators through a VR-based game. This innovative approach introduced a more immersive pathway for upskilling and reskilling. Early results demonstrate that the project successfully empowered educational staff, enabling them to acquire relevant skills, expand their knowledge, and remain up to date with technological advancements. © 2025 IEEE.
