AB  - This paper explores novel image synthesis techniques based on Generative Adversarial Networks (GAN). It begins with an overview of the fundamentals of GAN, its development history, and key innovative breakthroughs by 2025, including novel architectural designs and dataset extensions. Then the technological innovations are analyzed in detail, such as the application of augmented learning in GAN, the new exploration of the adversarial loss function, and the expansion of the technology's application in healthcare and virtual reality are discussed. Through the discussion of experimental methods and results, the performance of old and new models are compared, and successful cases in the field of art creation are shared. Finally, the future development trend is overlooked, while challenges such as data privacy protection are pointed out and possible solutions are proposed. This paper summarizes the main research findings and points out the limitations of the study and suggestions for follow-up work. © 2025 SPIE.
