AB  - In response to the challenges faced by general virtual product display systems when presenting artworks with high display effect requirements, such as the inability to fully showcase detailed features and poor display performance, this paper investigates and designs a virtual product display system based on visual communication and artificial intelligence algorithms. Based on the existing general display system, this systemintegrates image enhancement strategies from image processing technology and specifically employs advanced algorithms from the field of artificial intelligence, particularly Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs), to enhance image resolution while maintaining or improving detail representation. By introducing artificial intelligence algorithms, the system is able to handle image details, color adjustment and user interaction more intelligently, further enhancing the realism of the display effect and user experience. The experimental results show that the optimization system has a significant improvement in the overall display effect, detail performance and sense of reality, especially for the degree of product detail performance, the display effect is improved by 13.9%, reflecting the system’s strong ability in detail display. At the same time, the application of artificial intelligence algorithms also provides the system with more intelligent interaction and recommendation functions, so that it can better meet the needs of users, and provide a more efficient and intelligent display solution for virtual products such as artworks that require higher display effects. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s)
