TI  - RealitySummary: Exploring On-Demand Mixed Reality Text Summarization and Question Answering using Large Language Models
PY  - 2025
T2  - Proceedings - SUI 2025: ACM Symposium on Spatial User Interaction
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3694907.3765933
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105022942109?origin=resultslist
AB  - Large Language Models (LLMs) are gaining popularity as reading and summarization aids. However, little is known about their potential benefits when integrated with mixed reality (MR) interfaces to support everyday reading. In this iterative investigation, we developed RealitySummary 1, an MR reading assistant that seamlessly integrates LLMs with always-on camera access, OCR-based text extraction, and augmented spatial and visual responses. Developed iteratively, RealitySummary evolved across three versions, each shaped by user feedback and reflective analysis: 1) a preliminary user study to understand reader perceptions (N=12), 2) an in-the-wild deployment to explore real-world usage (N=11), and 3) a diary study to capture insights from real-world work contexts (N=5). Our empirical studies' findings highlight the unique advantages of combining AI and MR, including always-on implicit assistance, long-term temporal history, minimal context switching, and spatial affordances, demonstrating significant potential for future LLM-MR interfaces beyond traditional screen-based interactions. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
