TI  - Revolutionizing medical imaging and diagnostics through advanced AI and augmented reality technologies
PY  - 2025
T2  - Revolutionizing Digital Healthcare Through Artificial Intelligence and Automation: Principles, Technologies, and Applications
SP  - 597
EP  - 616
DO  - 10.1016/B978-0-443-36434-1.00037-9
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105023919076?origin=resultslist
AB  - This comprehensive review explores the transformative impact of advanced artificial intelligence (AI) algorithms and augmented reality (AR) technologies on medical imaging and diagnostics. We examine the rapid evolution of smart healthcare ecosystems, focusing on the paradigm shift from traditional medical imaging methods to AI-enhanced techniques. Our study introduces state-of-the-art deep learning models for analyzing diverse medical imaging modalities, demonstrating superior accuracy compared to both human experts and previous AI benchmarks. We delve into the integration of generative AI and AR systems for surgical planning and guidance, highlighting their potential to revolutionize medical procedures. The research addresses critical challenges in clinical implementation, including data privacy, algorithmic bias, and the need for explainable AI. We propose novel frameworks for interpretable AI in healthcare, ensuring transparency and trust in AI-driven diagnoses. Furthermore, we explore the synergistic potential of AI and AR when combined with emerging technologies such as 6G networks and edge computing. The paper concludes with a discussion on future prospects, ethical considerations, and the imperative for responsible innovation in healthcare AI. This review provides a comprehensive roadmap for researchers, clinicians, and policymakers navigating the rapidly evolving landscape of AI and AR in medical imaging and diagnostics. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. All rights reserved.
