AB  - Smart classroom Play and innovation in all corners of the world has emerged as a topic of study in the minds of educators of received wisdom of these 21 century where not only is the classroom characterized by the Conventional black board white boards but also by the inclusion of various competencies in the learning environment. Although engineering and technology possessed an enormous potential of revolutionizing the pedagogy of various sectors including math and sciences, the application of digitized technologies in visual arts pedagogy has not fully capitalized on the opportunities. The current paper explores the way through which arts education can be culturally transformed by the incorporation of engineering technologies into the pedagogy of the smart classrooms. Such a transformation is intrinsic with smart classrooms as a result of immersive, interactive and personalized learning experiences. Technology-driven classrooms that are small halls with multiple gadgets like interactive whiteboards, digital drawing tablets, virtual reality, augmented reality, artificial intelligence and collaborative technology in a real-time setting. These instruments have probably not only made the instruction and study of these arts much easier, and furnished us with harbingers of the future of creative expression in design, criticism and experimentation in the visual arts. In this regard the application of these technologies within the pedagogy of visual arts would free the visual artists educators up what we might call the studio. It remains to be mentioned that a hybrid approach toward teaching and learning may also exist, and to discover hands-on crafts and techniques may be paired with creativity and innovation in the domains of digital design and AI. This integration has a number of aspects of significance addressed in this paper. Partly, in this way, it explores the possibility of AR and VR to reproduce virtual art and virtual cabins at the same time in which the students will be able to interact with classical and modern works of art in three-dimensional spaces. These devices enable the learners to recreate an unequal collection of artistic means and to make attempts to utilize the style in a live department and to abstract the procedure of art and to explore more deeply the period of art and the context of art. Secondly, the paper is also devoted to the utilization of the engineering-based tools (digital fabrication and generative design software) to promote the illumination. You are the concept experiment of the human person, who offers his creative potential of the human creature unrestrained imagination admission to your software on the condition that he can reach the level of self-development, that is, to effective transition between aid thinking processes and outcome. © 2025 IEEE.
