AB  - This paper seeks to address the tourism and hospitality industry, encapsulating diverse themes ranging from cultural heritage preservation to the transformative potential of the metaverse in travel experiences. Emphasis is given to the cultural elements which strengthen a country’s tourism industry by attracting tourists and enhance competitiveness. Scholars explore the intricate interplay between heritage conservation and innovation through the lens of Cultural Inheritance-Based Innovation (CIBI), revealing its multifaceted influences by environmental, governmental, enterprise, and societal factors. Empirical evidence from longitudinal studies illuminates the profound impact of a country׳s cultural values on its competitiveness in the travel and tourism sector. Delving into the emergent phenomenon of metaverse tourism, researchers uncover empirical linkages between virtual travel experiences, telepresence, and future travel intentions. Additionally, inquiries into the integration of AI in hospitality and tourism highlight the burgeoning role of generative AI tools in enhancing customer experiences and operational efficiency, paving the way for sustainable tourism development. © 2026 Elsevier Inc. All rights are reserved, including those for text and data mining, AI training, and similar technologies.
