UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105025776614?origin=resultslist
AB  - This study aims to examine how artificial intelligence (AI) and virtual technologies enhance the design and creation process, with a specific focus on efficiency, collaboration, and decision-making in fields such as product development, engineering, and construction. It investigates how AI-driven design tools, including predictive modelling and generative design, along with immersive technologies like virtual reality (VR) and augmented reality (AR), are transforming traditional workflows. By employing sophisticated algorithms and machine learning approaches, these tools can evaluate enormous datasets, find trends, and produce efficient solutions based on performance criteria. Through real-world demonstrations and industrial applications. It highlights how these technologies improve design accuracy, reduce iteration time, and foster interdisciplinary collaboration. AI tools enable faster prototyping, customization of design solutions, and data-driven decisions, while VR/AR tools support interactive visualization and real-time feedback loops. These skills promote cost-effective and sustainable operations by significantly reducing design mistakes and resource waste. Intelligent automation improves design quality and expedites the process when paired with sophisticated modelling and ongoing user feedback. In collaborative design contexts, AI-powered technologies allow teams to communicate in real time, allowing for agile processes and synchronized changes. Incorporating these advances not only boosts creativity and efficiency but also helps set new benchmarks for digital design practice. The report examines how immersive environments are being utilized more often for user testing, training simulations, and stakeholder engagement, expanding their influence beyond the design stage. It concludes that the future of Computer-Aided Design (CAD) lies in the progressive development and adoption of AI and immersive tools, which empower designers to achieve higher innovation, adaptability, and collaboration in complex design environments. © 2025, Malque Publishing. All rights reserved.
