AB  - The rise of artificial intelligence (AI) avatars and engaging with natural communication in virtual environments has been explored widely to improve human-computer interaction. A virtual reality (VR) collaborative interface allows multiple users to collaborate in a virtual environment from different locations. It enables more than three users to meet up in the same shared space in a virtual environment and communicate verbally or non-verbally and through text or voice. The implementation of virtual environments in farming requires an attentive balance of technological advancement, agriculture, AI-based Simulations, and sustainability. By approaching this challenge, this study presents collaborative virtual farming with an AI avatar assistant, allowing multiple farmers or users to learn and discuss together in a shared space. Users or farmers can talk to the avatar as they would to an expert. The AI avatar can be tuned for different cultures, languages, and crops. Users did not just watch - they talked, tested, and learnt through guided practice, making sustainable agriculture both practical and engaging. Therefore, our AI avatar in our VR farming talks using voice and has its emotion detection, such as sad and happy. This paper explores the generative AI avatar for dynamic communication, involving speech for verbal communication to identify the emotion of player messages. © 2025 IEEE.
