TI  - Welding Bead Estimation with a Conditional Diffusion-based Generative Model for Constructing a VR Training Simulator
PY  - 2025
T2  - Journal of Information and Communication Convergence Engineering
VL  - 23
IS  - 2
SP  - 144
EP  - 153
DO  - 10.56977/jicce.2025.23.2.144
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105015847573?origin=resultslist
AB  - This study addresses the accurate prediction of weld-bead geometry, which is critical for improving weld quality, reducing potential defects, and optimizing operational efficiency. To overcome the challenges of traditional inverse models, we present a diffusion-based framework that incorporates temporal guidance through sequential frame data. Our model integrates a guidance encoder, latent transform with flow-based modeling, and a diffusion decoder to produce temporally consistent and structurally faithful 3D point clouds. The proposed model utilizes condition information to restore weld geometry data more accurately and its guided learning structure effectively supports overall shape preservation, spatial consistency, and time series-based continuous shape generation. Experiments showed that it outperforms standard diffusion methods using the PSNR, Chamfer distance, Jensen-Shannon divergence, and Hungarian error metrics. Qualitative results showed that the model maintains a balanced depiction of the global geometry without over-emphasizing areas with high point density. These results highlight potential applications in VR-based welding training systems and real-time adaptive control of automated welding processes. Copyright © The Korea Institute of Information and Communication Engineering.
