AB  - Yurt Portal is an interactive Extended Reality (XR) experience that augments physical space by generating and mirroring cultural digital twins to foster cross-cultural communication. Set in a yurt - a traditional Kyrgyz nomadic dwelling - the installation integrates physical objects from both Kyrgyz and Japanese cultures. Users engage with generative AI-powered digital twins of themselves and the objects, creating layered interactions between physical and virtual elements. The system comprises three key components: the yurt space, curated cultural objects, and AI-driven digital interactive augmentations. By situating virtual content within the physical environment, the project explores the reality-virtuality continuum, positioning XR not merely as a technological medium but as a cultural interface. Yurt Portal emphasizes empathy-based cultural learning [Geertz 2017] through familiar artifacts, encouraging deeper understanding between underrepresented and well-known cultures. It embedded cultural narratives into the continuum of XR, highlighting how familiarity can foster empathy and build respect for cultural differences. ©2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
