AB  - Addressing the problems of high material consumption, difficulty in practicing high-risk scenarios, and insufficient job adaptability in traditional prefabricated building decoration training, this study proposes a job-task-driven multimodal generative adversarial network (TGMF-GAN) to construct a VR training scene generation model. Guided by a job job map, the model integrates multimodal data from BIM components, practical videos, and skill texts. Through task-oriented attention fusion and dynamic fault-tolerant generation mechanisms, it achieves precise matching between job requirements and training scenarios. Experiments validated on a 12.8GB multimodal dataset showed that the job task matching rate of the TGMF-GAN-generated scenes reached 92.3%, with a VR rendering frame rate of 91.2fps. In terms of educational effectiveness, the skill attainment rate of the training group was 89.7% (a 37.6% improvement compared to the physical training group), the average cost per person decreased by 68.4%, and the skill forgetting rate was 12.8%. This model overcomes the bottlenecks of low efficiency and poor adaptability in traditional VR training modeling, providing a low-cost, high-efficiency, and safe intelligent solution for vocational education engineering training. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
