AB  - We propose AGYLIS (Autonomous Generative Yielding Lived-body Interaction System) as a human simulation framework in virtual reality, where AI dynamically generates gaze, decisions, and actions through an embodied avatar and achieves adaptive interactions with others and the environment. Based on this concept, we developed a simulation platform that enables multiple autonomous avatars to experience the same VR space. By comparing behavioral and experiential data obtained from human participants in an identical environment, we evaluated whether AGYLIS can reproduce human-like patterns of gaze and action. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
