AB  - Traditional storytelling is often constrained by linear structures, limiting engagement and interactivity. This research explores how AI-generated Mixed Reality (MR) environments can enhance storytelling through speech-driven interactions, realtime adaptive narratives, and Tactile feedback. The user's speech transforms real-world objects into AI-generated characters and 3D elements that shape the story. A playable MR game prototype using GPT-4 and Meshy. AI is developed to investigate how AI-generated storytelling elements integrate with physical space and influence user engagement. This research explores the intersection of Mixed Reality (MR), AI-driven storytelling, and interactive media, proposing an innovative MR-AI framework. © 2026 IEEE.
