AB  - With the rapid development of generative artificial intelligence (AIGC) technology, its applications in new media content production and dissemination have become increasingly widespread, particularly demonstrating significant potential in fashion communication. Addressing challenges such as high production costs, low efficiency, and difficulty in quantifying communication effectiveness in traditional fashion content creation, this study focuses on “AIGC-Assisted Fashion Content Generation and New Media Dissemination,” establishing an integrated analytical framework spanning content generation to dissemination evaluation. First, at the content production level, we achieve automated generation and style control of fashion visual content through diffusion models and text prompt engineering methods. Second, in dissemination analysis, we develop a multi-dimensional evaluation system encompassing click-through rates, like rates, comment rates, and share rates, while constructing a weighted scoring model for quantitative analysis of content dissemination performance. Finally, by comparing the dissemination effects of different content types and styles across new media platforms, we validate AIGC's advantages in enhancing content appeal and user engagement. Research findings indicate that AIGC-generated content significantly outperforms traditional content in key metrics such as click-through rates and interaction rates, effectively improving dissemination efficiency and user participation while demonstrating stronger adaptability in innovative style expression. This study not only expands the application pathways of AIGC in fashion communication but also provides data-driven theoretical foundations and practical references for optimizing content production and dissemination in new media environments.
