AB  - While current entertainment XR platforms have achieved significant immersion, there remains a need for more integrated emotional adaptation and self-regulation mechanisms. To explore this, this paper proposes an Adaptive Immersive Learning & Self-Regulation Framework. Experiments show that the emotion recognition accuracy of this model under high cognitive load is 94.5%, which is better than that of the single mode. In terms of physiological empowerment, the system can guide the user's electrodermal activity (EDA) value to return from a 9.5 μS surge state to a 5 μS benchmark within 180 s, generating a recovery gain of approximately 2.5 μS. The user's frustration score, measured on a 0–100 NASA-TLX scale, dropped from 82 to 30. The wrong operation rate decreased by 18.4%. The results show that the system can effectively enhance immersion and provide immediate, assisted emotional regulation within the virtual environment © 2026 Published by Elsevier B.V.
