AB  - By February 2026, leading generative AI models, including international ones such as Nano Banana Pro, Sora2, and Gemini3, as well as domestic ones like Deepseek, Keling, and Doudou, have already transformed the art creation landscape in a very clear and substantial way: AI tools have evolved from text-only generators to multimodal creators capable of generating images, videos, and prompt-based solutions. More importantly, the relevant models have advanced from producing random outputs to generating results with physical consistency and logical visual reasoning. Thus the intelligent agent workflow is turning creators into directors, and a new “human-agent” collaborative framework is emerging, where agents function as autonomous entities with well-designed feedback loops.
