TI  - Computer Vision and Deep Learning-Driven Intelligent Animation IP Creation: A Case Study of Zhong Kui Character Design Based on AI Intelligent Drawing
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of the 2nd International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Virtual Reality and Interaction Design
SP  - 537
EP  - 542
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3820915.3820997
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3820915.3820997
AB  - Against the backdrop of the deep integration of computer vision (CV), deep learning (DL) and generative artificial intelligence (AIGC) in the animation industry, and in response to the core theme of the 2nd International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Virtual Reality and Interaction Design (AIVRID 2026) — “Computer Vision and Image Processing, Deep Learning and AI Intelligent Drawing”, this study aims to address the prominent industry pain points in animation IP development, including insufficient creative capacity, low efficiency of image processing, and difficult management of cross-media style consistency. With the rapid development of AI technology, animation IP creation is facing an urgent demand for intelligent transformation, while traditional manual design models and single AI drawing methods can no longer meet the requirements of high efficiency, high quality and cultural consistency in modern animation IP development [1]. Focusing on the synergistic adaptation between intelligent character design and worldview construction, which is a key link in animation IP creation, this research takes the classic traditional Chinese cultural image Zhong Kui as the research carrier, and takes the creation of its animated character and supporting 30-second short film as the core case, constructing a CV-DL dual-drive intelligent animation IP design framework deeply integrated with AI intelligent drawing technology. Specifically, computer vision technology, including image preprocessing, SIFT feature extraction and image matching algorithms, is used to accurately extract the cultural feature elements of Zhong Kui from 500 traditional artworks (such as paintings, murals and sculptures), establishing a standardized cultural feature library to ensure the inheritance of traditional cultural connotations [2]. Meanwhile, deep learning models represented by StyleGAN2 are employed to realize intelligent generation and multi-dimensional optimization of character shapes, textures and dynamic effects, and the model is trained through 100,000 iterations to improve the clarity and authenticity of generated images [16]. The experimental results show that the proposed framework can significantly improve the efficiency and quality of animation IP creation, and effectively ensure the consistency of character image and worldview style. Compared with traditional manual design methods, the design cycle of animation characters is shortened by 62.3%, the average feature similarity between generated characters and traditional cultural images reaches 87.9%, and the user satisfaction rate among 50 professional evaluators reaches 89.7%. This research not only provides a feasible technical path for the intelligent transformation of animation IP creation, enriches the application scenarios of computer vision and deep learning in the cultural and creative field, but also responds to the development trend of the integration of computer technology and animation industry emphasized by AIVRID 2026, providing important academic reference for the innovative application of AI intelligent drawing technology in animation IP creation [17].
