AB  - Professional piano practice often lacks immediate and expressive feedback when conducted without an instructor or collaborative partner. This pilot study explores how immersive and generative technologies can enhance advanced piano training through CoPianist, a virtual reality system integrating generative AI for MIDI-based guidance and virtual hand simulation. The system combines adaptive MIDI performance generation with synchronized virtual hand movements, allowing learners to observe and co-perform with a virtual pianist on a simulated piano. Using hand tracking and realtime MIDI analysis, CoPianist delivers feedback on note accuracy, tempo stability, and technical execution. © 2026 IEEE.
