AB  - This paper introduces a VR system for precise anxiety intervention, integrating LLM, Generative AI, and Unreal Engine 5.5 on Quest 3. Unlike generic apps, it employs a semi-automated pipeline to construct personalized 3D environments from user interviews, featuring a conversational virtual friend for support. A 6-user preexperience indicates intervention effectiveness correlates strongly with anxiety type. For specific phobias in realistic exposure scenes, the virtual friend acted as a vital emotional anchor, significantly outperforming traditional relaxation. Conversely, for general anxiety, interactions provided improvement but lacked deep dependency induction. These findings suggest that virtual social companionship holds significantly greater therapeutic weight in high-stress contexts, offering key insights for future adaptive VR psychotherapy. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
