TI  - Developing Active Learning Environments: AI-Enhanced Open-Source VR for Semiconductor Manufacturing
PY  - 2026
T2  - 2026 49th MIPRO ICT and Electronics Convention, MIPRO 2026 - Proceedings
SP  - 547
EP  - 551
DO  - 10.1109/MIPRO70003.2026.11591682
SN  - 1847-3938
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105046159531?origin=resultslist
AB  - Virtual Reality (VR) models based on open-source software, in combination with CAD/CAM 3D models, are emerging as a possible vital engineering education tool to address the severe semiconductor workforce shortage. These accessible and cost-effective digital twins, often built using platforms like Godot and incorporating AI-powered tutors (LLMs), create an active educational learning environment in virtual cleanrooms. This paper presents a research-question-driven literature review of VR/XR environments, CAD/CAM-integrated virtual workflows, digital twins and AI-powered tutors applied to semiconductor manufacturing education. The selected studies are organised around three questions: how VR/CAD platforms affect accessibility and scalability of engineering education, how VR simulations with or without AI tutors compare to traditional cleanroom-based training, and how digital twins contribute to risk reduction, training cost and design-quality improvements. The review shows consistent benefits in engagement, procedural understanding and training efficiency, while also highlighting that semiconductor package and design training, and the combination of VR with domain-specific AI tutors, remain underexplored areas for future classroom implementation. © 2026 IEEE.
