AB  - We present DNA-MESS, a closed-loop adaptive VR system that dynamically adjusts narrative and sensory feedback based on users' physiological and behavioral states. A custom hybrid headset integrating PPG sensing, bone-conduction audio, and haptics enables real-time affect-responsive interaction. Signals are processed in Unity and mapped to generative AI-driven adaptations of audio, haptics, and environmental parameters. Unlike existing systems that rely on behavioral inputs or single modalities, DNA-MESS demonstrates a unified multi-modal sensing-feedback pipeline. The system is showcased through an interactive VR horror demo, illustrating the design space of emotionally adaptive virtual environments. © 2026 IEEE.
