AB  - With the rapid development of virtual reality technology, its application in the field of intelligent design has attracted wide attention. This paper aims to explore the path of user experience optimization and its empirical effect of virtual reality technology in the field of intelligent design. Through literature review and theoretical analysis, a theoretical framework for improving user experience in virtual reality environment is proposed. In the experiment, 122 subjects were selected, qualitative and quantitative methods were used, and a virtual reality interactive platform was built based on Unity3D engine for comparative evaluation. The platform adopts a hybrid rendering pipeline of forward rendering and deferred rendering, with a fixed rendering frame rate of 90 FPS and a dynamic resolution scaling threshold of 0.8–1.0. Compared with traditional VR experience optimization methods that rely on manual parameter adjustment and single-modal interaction design, this study introduces a few-shot learning algorithm based on ResNet-18 feature extraction and cosine similarity classifier, which can realize fast user role modeling with small sample size and avoid the problem of insufficient training data caused by high cost of VR user behavior collection. Meanwhile, the generative adversarial network (GAN) used in the process intelligence layer breaks through the limitation that traditional design methods can only carry out fixed scheme iteration, and realizes the autonomous evolution of interactive schemes driven by user perception data. The results show that compared with the traditional media, the virtual reality environment has significantly improved the information acceptance effect, immersion and participation. Combined with few-shot learning algorithm based on ResNet-18 feature extraction and cosine similarity classifier, support set K=5, query set M=10, training epoch=30, learning rate=1 10⁻⁴, the contribution of different user role models to experience design optimization is verified. The comprehensive analysis shows that the user experience improvement path of virtual reality with user needs as the core has important theoretical and application value in the field of intelligent design.
