TI  - Fading Peach Blossom Spring: A Perspective-Shifting VR Narrative with Reactive 3D Gaussian Splatting
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of the Special Interest Group on Computer Graphics and Interactive Techniques Conference Posters
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3799825.3818737
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3799825.3818737
AB  - 3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) has enabled high-fidelity scene reconstruction, yet its applications in virtual reality have remained largely limited to static visualization. We present Fading Peach Blossom Spring, a stylized VR interactive narrative that combines generative AI, 3DGS, and Unreal Engine to create an environment that changes irreversibly through user interaction. Inspired by the classical Chinese tale The Peach Blossom Spring, the work constructs a perspective-shifting experience in which users first explore an idyllic ink-wash world that gradually dissolves into a desolate alternative space through touch. To realize this experience, we propose a reactive representation and interaction pipeline that transforms static 3DGS into a particle-based system for real-time environmental change, enabling a destructive interaction paradigm in which touch drives both environmental decay and narrative transition. User feedback suggests that this design encourages reflection on loss, responsibility, and the consequences of intervention. Overall, this work demonstrates the potential of 3DGS as a reactive medium for stylized VR storytelling and agency-driven narrative interaction.
