DO  - 10.1145/3820915.3821123
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3820915.3821123
AB  - Abstract-This study addresses the inefficiency and limited interaction quality of traditional embedded UI development by proposing a closed-loop, constraint-aware generative framework for rapid interface generation and interaction validity verification. Unlike existing approaches that focus solely on UI generation, the proposed method integrates intent understanding, structured constraint modeling, hardware-aware rendering, and interaction feedback optimization into a unified pipeline. Specifically, the framework introduces a “describe-generate-interact-optimize” loop, which transforms multimodal user input into executable UI interfaces under strict embedded hardware constraints. For reproducibility, hardware constraints are encoded as a JSON device profile and injected into generation through prompt templates plus a rule-based verifier, rather than end-to-end retraining. To ensure practical usability, a multi-level validation scheme is designed, combining static feasibility checks, dynamic performance testing, and user-centered evaluation. A case study based on a smart thermostat interface demonstrates that the proposed method achieves order-of-magnitude improvements in development efficiency, while maintaining comparable task performance and significantly improving user experience. The results indicate that the framework provides a verifiable and scalable paradigm for embedded UI development, bridging the gap between generative AI capabilities and real-world human-computer interaction requirements.
