AB  - Generative AI can accelerate VR animation production in classrooms by supporting tasks such as storyboarding, shot planning, and critique preparation. Yet classroom adoption raises a design problem: how can AI-supported production remain aligned with learning objectives, interpretable to students, and governable by teachers? This paper presents Rubrics-to-Guardrails, a platform-agnostic design framework that translates course rubrics into operational constraints, validation gates, feedback triggers, and governance actions for VR animation production classrooms. The paper contributes a workflow specification with two explicit decision gates, a four-layer framework, design guidelines, a rubric-to-guardrails mapping checklist, and a structured walkthrough of selected representative failure scenarios. Rather than claiming outcome effects, the study provides proof-of-concept and process-level feasibility evidence for integrating generative AI into VR animation classrooms while maintaining teacher oversight, lightweight accountability, and pedagogical flexibility. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
