AB  - In this paper, we introduce GAVIA-X, an extension of the GAVIA framework that transforms a methodology for Generative AI (GenAI) content extension into an interactive visualization and correction mechanism for the generation of 3D environments from Large Language Model (LLM) prompts for Virtual and Mixed Realities (VR/XR). The main contribution is a novel system that overcomes the challenges of Diffusion models to produce smooth and consistent 360° panoramic cubemaps by involving a Gemma-based LLM to automatically generate contextual prompts and an interactive, VR/XR-ready inpainting mechanism through an A-Frame plug-in. Based on an A-Frame plugin, the system provides a VR/XR experience in which users can 'paint' masks on the 3D cubemap face in order to fix GenAI artifacts, or customize scenes, and employs morphological operators (dilation and closing) to smooth the masks and produce seamless transitions for a better VR/XR. The most promising use cases are the generation of customized datasets for World Models (WM) training and synthetic backgrounds, facilitating the training with human supervision. © 2026 IEEE.
