PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3774521.3774603
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105047003856?origin=resultslist
AB  - This paper introduces a novel mixed-reality (MR) 3D authoring platform designed to enable real-time, interactive composition of 3D scenes in augmented and mixed reality environments. The platform proposed and integrates two key innovations: a three-tier 3D asset generation workflow and a 3D sketch-to-shape retrieval algorithm. The three-tier architecture addresses the challenge of time-consuming 3D asset creation by allowing users to engage with the generation process at intermediate stages, enabling rapid validation and refinement of user inputs. This approach not only enhances interactivity but also accelerates the realization of user imagined assets. Complementing this is our 3D sketch-to-shape retrieval system, which leverages an intuitive, robust sketching module to query a library of generated or artist-created 3D assets. This mechanism facilitates precise retrieval of objects matching both the category and rough shape of a user drawn 3D sketch of the assets. The platform supports multi-modal, intuitive user inputs such as speech, text, and freehand 3D sketches, making it accessible to both novice and expert users for creating, retrieving, modifying, and composing 3D assets and textures. By combining generative models with intuitive interaction, the platform serves as a flexible testbed for 3D asset development and a tool to democratize 3D scene authoring. We show effectiveness of GeMR on various use-cases, including scenario composition for human-robot collaboration. We conducted a user study to evaluate whether our system effectively democratizes the 3D scene composition. We compared the performance of 3D modeling experts and novice users on a standardized scene creation task. Both novice and expert users reported equally good usability ratings and low perceived workload. Our findings highlight that an integration of generative models and multimodal intuitive inputs represents a significant leap in making the 3D scene authoring more accessible. © 2025 