AB  - Biophilic design, which integrates natural elements into built environments, has been shown to support cognitive, affective, and physical well-being in older adults. However, physical biophilic interventions are costly, space-intensive, and often difficult to retrofit in senior living facilities. This paper presents a generative AI-supported augmented reality (AR) approach for biophilic design, enabling seniors to experience personalized and scalable biophilic environments. We developed a four-stage prompting pipeline to generate diverse 3D biophilic assets, which were integrated into a Unity-based AR application deployable on mobile and tablet devices. A preliminary pilot experiment with two participants explored cognitive and affective responses using Stroop and PANAS measures, alongside exit surveys capturing user perceptions. Results indicated individual variability in cognitive responses, stable affective states across conditions, and generally positive evaluations of the biophilic AR environment. These findings provide proof-of-concept evidence for the feasibility and experiential potential of generative AI-supported biophilic AR in senior living contexts. Future work will involve larger cohorts, validated usability measures, and comparative evaluation with physical biophilic environments. © 2026 ASCE.
