DO  - 10.1109/IEHNS68708.2026.11606934
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105047954566?origin=resultslist
AB  - This study proposes a human-AI collaborative framework to resolve the tension between technological innovation and depth of cultural transmission in heritage communication, exemplified through the intelligent dissemination of traditional Chinese tea culture. By integrating generative artificial intelligence and augmented reality, the framework employs a four-dimensional cultural genome indexing system spanning architectural, material, behavioral, and spiritual layers to enable progressive narrative exploration - from tea-ceremony utensils to ritual practices and philosophical principles. AR-driven virtual reconstruction of historical tea culture and large language model-enhanced dialogue interfaces transform passive consumption into dynamic co-creation, where users actively shape cultural meanings through natural language engagement. Self-optimizing mechanisms dynamically align technological outputs with the depth of cultural transmission by synthesizing multi-source feedback, user interactions, curator oversight, and ethical validation, thereby resolving the imbalance where technological spectacle overshadows substantive cultural transmission. Positioning AI as an amplifier of human expertise, the framework offers solutions for heritage preservation, harmonizing computational power with cultural intentionality to foster immersive, ethically grounded engagement. © 2026 IEEE.
