TI  - LaserCoPilot: A Transferable Multimodal Co-pilot for Closed-Loop Installation and Assembly Guidance via Step-Indexed Laser Projection
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of the International Symposium on Automation and Robotics in Construction
SP  - 137
EP  - 144
DO  - 10.22260/ISARC2026/0019
UR  - https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105046009203?origin=resultslist
AB  - Manual assembly in construction and manufacturing currently relies on static instructions (manuals, SOPs) that are brittle to variability and lack real-time feedback. To address this, we present a laser-based multimodal co-pilot that delivers dynamic, closed-loop guidance in non-wearable settings. The proposed framework compiles heterogeneous documentation (manuals, CAD/BIM) into a unified representation containing a step graph and verifiable criteria. At runtime, the system fuses user intent, scene perception, and uncertainty modeling to generate synchronized natural-language guidance and actionable laser cues. Crucially, it performs post-action verification to assess quality and issue targeted corrections, while maintaining persistent session memory for automated reporting. Proof-of-concept validation demonstrates the system’s feasibility for interactive guidance, grounded Q&A, and robust quality verification. © 2026 International Association on Automation and Robotics in Construction. All Rights Reserved.
