AB  - The integration of Large Language Models (LLMs) into Extended Reality (XR) has significantly increased energy demands and carbon emissions during inference. Despite this, most users remain unaware of the environmental footprint of their AI interactions. To bridge this gap, we introduce LOCOMO-Play (LOwer COnsumption, More Optimization), a gamified Augmented Reality application designed to promote sustainable AI habits by gamifying prompt optimization. The application transforms the technical task of prompt optimization into a playful user experience by providing carbon footprint comparisons and rewarding users with Sustainability Points for crafting concise, energy-efficient prompts. This work demonstrates how gamification in XR can effectively align user behavior with sustainability goals in the era of generative AI. Click here for the demo video. © 2026 IEEE.
