AB  - We present Lumina-HT2, an AI-augmented virtual reality system for efficient lifelog retrieval in the Lifelog Search Challenge 2026. Building on Lumina-1, the proposed system introduces a human-AI collaborative framework that assists users with real-time search tasks. Lumina-HT2 integrates a temporal indexing engine and optimized data handling (caching and prefetching) to reduce latency in multi-step queries, and leverages multimodal fusion across visual, activity, location, and biometric data to improve retrieval accuracy. An LLM-based query planner enables automatic query decomposition and proactive suggestions, supporting users in complex search scenarios. Our experiments with volunteers on the LSC'26 dataset demonstrate improved performance in temporal retrieval while maintaining strong efficiency in atomic queries, highlighting the effectiveness of combining VR interaction with AI-driven assistance. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
