AB  - The concept of 'Modulated Reality (MoR),' which modulates space through the interaction between a real object in real space and an aerial image displayed using an AR device placed in front of it, has been proposed. However, the optical characteristics necessary for implementation have not been clarified, and at present it is not easy to systematize and utilize MoR as a new 3D display method. In this study, we aim to establish the optical characteristics required for systemization by clarifying the relationship between a real object and an aerial image in terms of luminance, and to implement a simplified MoR display by utilizing depth maps generated with generative AI. Through evaluation experiments, we clarified the relationship between absolute luminance and depth perception, providing the foundation for implementing MoR displays beyond the constraints of time and location. © 2026 IEEE.
