AB  - This paper presents SmartAgent, a real-time multimodal framework that integrates Large Language Models (LLMs), speech processing, and embodied avatar rendering to enable more natural and expressive human-computer interaction. The system introduces an embodied conversational agent, Bitzy, capable of interpreting user input and responding through synchronized speech, facial expressions, gestures, and gaze. To ensure consistency across modalities, a structured JSON schema is used to bridge cognitive processing and real-time animation in Unity. The architecture adopts a modular design that decouples speech recognition, language generation, and rendering, improving scalability and responsiveness. Preliminary results indicate that the proposed approach enhances user engagement, perceived presence, and interaction quality when compared to traditional text-based interfaces. These findings suggest that multimodal embodied agents represent a promising direction for developing more human-centered interactive systems. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
