AB  - This paper reports on the launch of a real-time AI-assisted virtual interviewer panel that is intended to simulate human-like interviewer behaviour using multimodal analysis and psychological modeling. Current platforms commonly incorporate AI technology but do not demonstrate emotional intelligence and thus, lack the ability to demonstrate realism and better accuracy in assessment. This new model combines Natural Language Processing, Speech Analytics, Computer Vision, and Biofeedback Sensing to analyse both communication and signs of stress. The panel embraces Eysenck's Personality Theory with three basic types of AI interviewers - friendly, analytical, and strict -that modulate based on responses in each session adaptively. The employed Large Language Models (LLM) and Virtual Reality Exposure Therapy, enhance realism while providing the candidate, a familiar high-fidelity experience to assist with anxiety and develop confidence prior to job interviews. This research explores an example of how AI and psychology can create a more immersive and emotionally intelligent interview experience. © 2026 IEEE.
