TI  - Research on the Differentiated Communication Paradigm of Film and Television Content Driven by Intelligent Image Generation and Multimodal Interaction
PY  - 2026
T2  - Proceedings of the 2nd International Conference on Artificial Intelligence, Virtual Reality and Interaction Design
SP  - 803
EP  - 808
PB  - Association for Computing Machinery
DO  - 10.1145/3820915.3821039
UR  - https://doi.org/10.1145/3820915.3821039
AB  - The iterative evolution of artificial intelligence technology has profoundly reshaped the ecological landscape of film and television production and communication. The dual drive of intelligent image generation and multimodal interaction technologies has enabled the film and television industry to break through the constraints of traditional standardized production and mass communication, making differentiated communication a core trend of film and television communication in the intelligent era. The two technologies respectively realize the efficient customization of differentiated content and the in-depth reconstruction of the audience's viewing experience, and jointly drive the transformation of film and television communication from a “content-centered” model to an “audience-centered” one. From the interdisciplinary perspective of technology and communication, this paper sorts out the media evolution and contemporary driving forces of differentiated film and television communication, combines 12 typical industrial cases of AI film and television creation from 2024 to 2025 and the user behavior data of 3 major video platforms (Tencent Video, Douyin, Kuaishou) with a sample size of 500,000+, quantitatively analyzes the implementation effect and industrial application value of differentiated communication, expounds the core connotation and operational logic of this paradigm in the dimensions of content creation, channel communication and experience interaction, and provides a systematic cognitive framework for understanding the transformative characteristics of film and television communication in the intelligent era.With the continuous maturity of large-scale pre-trained models and generative artificial intelligence technologies, the integration of technology and film and television content has entered a deep-water area. Unlike the previous single auxiliary application, the current intelligent image generation and multimodal interaction technologies have realized the whole-chain penetration from script creation, scene rendering, post-production to interactive experience design. Differentiated communication, as an important communication strategy to adapt to the fragmentation and personalization of audience needs, has gradually evolved from a theoretical concept to a mainstream industrial practice. In this context, it is of great theoretical and practical significance to systematically explore the paradigm characteristics, operation logic and development challenges of differentiated communication driven by dual technologies. This paper attempts to fill the research gap of insufficient systematic research on the whole chain of differentiated communication in the existing literature, and provide reference for the high-quality development of China's film and television industry in the intelligent era.
