AB  - This work presents a VR karaoke experience that treats voice as an affective input for immersive environmental feedback. Vocal and musical affect function as joint control signals mapped to generative visual dynamics in a virtual forest. Arousal and valence modulate growth, color, and atmospheric change, allowing singers to perceive how expressive variation shapes the environment in real time. The system explores affect-driven music interaction in VR, encouraging performers to experiment with vocal expression through responsive visual feedback aligned with the song’s emotional progression. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
