AB  - Designing expressive haptic feedback in XR remains challenging due to limited authoring tools and high expertise barriers. We address this through two complementary systems: HapticPilot, a VR-based toolkit for posture-aware haptic sketching that adapts vibrotactile designs across dynamic hand configurations, and HapticGen, the first text-to-vibration generative model optimized via expert preference alignment. Together, these systems reduce iteration costs, lower the entry barrier for novice designers, and support scalable tactile content creation. This work further lays the groundwork for multimodal, context-aware haptic generation that integrates cross-modal cues for adaptive and personalized tactile experiences in XR. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
