AB  - Addressing the cultural heritage protection dilemma caused by prolonged deterioration of ancient architectural complexes in the Shanwei region, this paper proposes a virtual restoration method for ancient buildings based on Generative Adversarial Networks (GANs). The Pix2Pix network architecture is improved to adapt to architectural restoration tasks by introducing attention mechanisms and multi-scale feature fusion to enhance restoration quality. The experiment selected 12 typical ancient buildings in Shanwei City for virtual restoration simulation, including ancestral halls, temples, and traditional residences, constructing a dataset containing 2,400 high-resolution images. Experimental results demonstrate that the improved GAN model achieves a Peak Signal-to-Noise Ratio (PSNR) of 28.347 dB, Structural Similarity Index (SSIM) of 0.921, and Fréchet Inception Distance (FID) of 15.683, representing improvements of 12.3%, 8.7%, and 34.2% respectively compared to baseline methods. The user experience score reaches 4.62/5.00. The virtual restoration system has been deployed on the Shanwei cultural tourism platform, achieving digital preservation and immersive cultural experience of ancient buildings, providing technical support for cultural heritage protection in eastern Guangdong. © 2025 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
