AB  - We present a novel system that reimagines how users create and deliver presentations within extended reality (XR). Beyond static 2D slides, our approach enables presenters to generate images or 3D objects dynamically using natural language input, supporting immersive storytelling and interactive Q&A in real time. The system leverages a modular architecture combining voice or text input, a WebGPU-enabled frontend for local AI inference, and a backend MCP-based pipeline for text-to-image-to-3D generation. The prototype demonstrates how presenters can create museum-like or spatially rich presentations, respond to unexpected questions with new visualizations, and explore spontaneous content generation within an XR environment. © 2026 IEEE.
