AB  - This paper presents the design rationale and prototype of a Stress Resilience Simulator for Healthcare Assistants, an immersive learning environment that addresses emotionally demanding workplace interactions and stress-related attrition in nursing. Grounded in evidence that verbally challenging and emotionally charged interactions are prevalent, harmful, and amenable to communication and regulation training, the simulator fuses extended reality (XR), generative AI, and biofeedback to build emotional self-control and communication competence. The system comprises three interoperable components: (1) the Challenger, which stages realistic, risk-free social encounters with patients and relatives, enabling repeated, personalized practice of de-escalation strategies via AI-driven, naturalistic dialogue; (2) the Trainer, which delivers heart-rate-variability biofeedback within restorative virtual nature scenes, embedding physiological signals directly into the environment to scaffold regulation skills; and (3) the Coach, which provides psychoeducation, adaptive guidance, progress tracking, and gamified feedback based on physiological and psychometric indicators. The project targets measurable gains in acute stress regulation, transfer of trained communication and regulation behaviors to practice, and learner satisfaction, with longer-term aims of improving well-being, training quality, and retention. © ISES 2026.
